{
  "id": "COMPOUND:30153 - PROTEIN:5854",
  "verbalization": "Methyl Lucidenate Q appears to have multiple targets that ultimately lead to the cell line LNCaP, suggesting a complex network of interactions. The first pathway links Methyl Lucidenate Q to Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9, which is targeted by a specific compound, and this target further interacts with LNCaP. The second and third pathways connect Methyl Lucidenate Q to another enzyme, CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, which is also targeted by Leosibirone B, and both of these targets ultimately interact with LNCaP. These findings suggest that Methyl Lucidenate Q may act through multiple distinct pathways, each involving different enzymes that ultimately contribute to the interaction with LNCaP. The evidence supports a mechanism where Methyl Lucidenate Q influences cellular processes through various enzymes, potentially affecting LNCaP through different molecular mechanisms.",
